d analysis\u003C/resp>\u003C/respStmt>\n            \u003C/titleStmt>\n            \u003CpublicationStmt>\n                \u003Cauthority>I.Sicily\u003C/authority>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"filename\">ISic000693\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"TM\">175752\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDR\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDH\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDCS\">6100261\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"PHI\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"URI\">http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic000693\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"DOI\" when=\"2020-12-22\">10.5281/zenodo.4385178\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cavailability>\n                    \u003Clicence target=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\">Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.\u003C/licence>\n                \u003C/availability>\n            \u003C/publicationStmt>\n            \u003CsourceDesc>\n                \u003CmsDesc>\n                    \u003CmsIdentifier>\n                        \u003Ccountry>Italy\u003C/country>\n                        \u003Cregion>Sicily\u003C/region>\n                        \u003Csettlement>Tindari\u003C/settlement>\n                        \u003Crepository role=\"museum\" ref=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/052\">Antiquarium di Tindari\u003C/repository>\n                        \u003C!--No inventory number found-->\n                        \u003C!--Adding location for old id numbers if available-->\n                        \u003CaltIdentifier>\n                            \u003Csettlement/>\n                            \u003Crepository/>\n                            \u003Cidno type=\"old\"/>\n                        \u003C/altIdentifier>\n                    \u003C/msIdentifier>\n                    \u003CmsContents>\n                        \u003CtextLang mainLang=\"la\">Latin\u003C/textLang>\n                    \u003C/msContents>\n                    \u003CphysDesc>\n                        \u003CobjectDesc>\n                            \u003CsupportDesc>\n                                \u003Csupport>\u003Cp>A tablet of yellowish stone with pinkish red veins running through it. The tablet is broken into at least 6 fragments and has been recomposed and mounted on a stand. Intact on all sides, but with a hole upper middle where one fragment is lost. The edges are straight, but the rear is very rough and irregular.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Cmaterial ana=\"#material.inorganic.stone.sedimentary_rock.limestone.calcite_limestone.yellow.calcare-lucidabile_giallo_giallo-antico\" type=\"stone.limestone.polishable.yellow\" subtype=\"giallo-antico-chemtou\" resp=\"#Coccato\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html\">brecciated yellow limestone with reddish veins, likely (microcrystalline limestone with sanidine crystals, opaque minerals veins, and sparry patches) (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy, XRD, optical microscopy)\n\u003CplaceName type=\"provenance\">\n \u003Cref target=\"https://www.geonames.org/11904191/chemtou.html\">Chemtou\u003C/ref>\n \u003Clocation>\n  \u003Cgeo>36.52736,8.58599\u003C/geo>\n \u003C/location>\n\u003C/placeName>\u003C/material>\n                                    \u003CobjectType ana=\"#object.plaque\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259\">plaque\u003C/objectType>\n                                    \u003Cdimensions>\n                                        \u003Cheight unit=\"cm\">28\u003C/height>\n                                        \u003Cwidth unit=\"cm\">29.4\u003C/width>\n                                        \u003Cdepth unit=\"cm\">max 4.1\u003C/depth>\n                                    \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003C/support>\n                                \u003Ccondition ana=\"#condition.complete.broken\"/>\n\t\t    \u003C/supportDesc>\n                            \u003ClayoutDesc>\n                                \u003Clayout>\u003Cp>Four lines of Latin letters approximately centred on the stone and reducing in height.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Crs ana=\"#execution.chiselled\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1\">chiselled\u003C/rs>\n                                \t\u003Cdamage ana=\"#text_condition.complete\"/>\n\t\t\t\u003C/layout>\n                            \u003C/layoutDesc>\n                        \u003C/objectDesc>\n                        \u003ChandDesc>\n                            \u003ChandNote>\u003Cp>A moderately deep v-cut, with wide modules in lines 1-2, narrower in line 3. Letters have pronounced but simple wedge serifs, and pronounced curvature on Y and X. The interpuncts in line 3 (only) have the form of hederae.\u003C/p>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line1\" to=\"line1\">Line 1\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"50\" atMost=\"50\">50\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line2\" to=\"line2\">Line 2\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"44\" atMost=\"46\">44-46 (Y=50)\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line3\" to=\"line3\">Line 3\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"37\" atMost=\"45\">37-45\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line4\" to=\"line4\">Line 4\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"30\" atMost=\"30\">30\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line1\" to=\"line2\">Interlineation line 1 to 2\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"interlinear\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\"/>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                            \u003C/handNote>\n                        \u003C/handDesc>\n                    \u003C/physDesc>\n                    \u003Chistory>\n                        \u003Corigin>\n                            \u003CorigPlace>\u003Cregion>Sicilia\u003C/region>\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"ancient\" ref=\"http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462527\">Tyndaris\u003C/placeName>\t\t\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"modern\" ref=\"http://sws.geonames.org/10282151\">Tindari\u003C/placeName>\n                            \t\u003Cgeo>38.14227, 15.04385\u003C/geo>\n\t\t\u003C/origPlace>\n                            \u003CorigDate datingMethod=\"#julian\" notBefore-custom=\"0101\" notAfter-custom=\"0200\" evidence=\"lettering\">second century CE\u003C/origDate>\n                        \u003C/origin>\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"found\" subtype=\"discovered\" when=\"1956\">From tomb 25, one of 69 burials in a necropolis of the period C1 BCE - C2 CE excavated in 1956 in contrada Scozzo (immediately outside the main gate on the southern side of the city) by Ferruccio Barreca. The burial contained votive terracottas, ceramic relief medalions, and glass perfume bottles.\u003Cgeo cert=\"high\">38.1416969,15.0421195\u003C/geo>\u003C/provenance>\u003C!-- centrepoint of the cda Scozzo necropolis -->\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"observed\" subtype=\"autopsied\" resp=\"#JP\" xml:id=\"autopsy\">Prag 2022-07-14, in the Antiquari